      "writtenOn": "2025-02-24T11:07:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The max number of immediates is hardcoded in some frontend data structures so we can put this logic in the frontend like kMaxBindGroups. https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/Limits.cpp;drc\u003da04b6a4f5e0447f04513cfd2305b6460345972e0;l\u003d338\n\nThe Vulkan limits are guaranteed to be much bigger at 128. So here we can hardcode that it is kMaxImmediateBytes, and have checks like these with comments explaining that if they break, we are using too many push constants in the worst case.\n\n```\nconstexpr uint32_t kMinVulkanPushConstants \u003d 128;\nDAWN_ASSERT(vkLimits.maxPushConstantsSize \u003e\u003d kMinVulkanPushConstants);\nstatic_assert(kMinVulkanPushConstants  \u003e\u003d sizeof(RenderImmediateConstants));\n// same for compute\n```",
      "revId": "334f58284607f2f75b8cdb7731a1536567e47a8e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
